        "content": "**Adult daycare services** give frail or impaired adults supervised care while the principal caregiver is away. You will usually see weekday schedules that match a workday, so a caregiver can drop off the client on the commute and pick them up after work. These programs may offer social time, medical care, therapy, or dementia-focused support. In practice, you help clients compare the setting and extra fees against home care or facility care."
