    "heading": "4.1 People Need to Plan for Long-term Care",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Planning ahead** for long-term care matters because many people will need some level of help after age 65, and the chance rises as they get older. If you wait until a crisis, you lose choices. When you help clients plan early, you give them time to compare services, check eligibility rules, and understand what care costs in their community. That matters because most families cannot simply pay for extended care from income alone. Early planning can also protect a spouse’s lifestyle, preserve some assets for heirs, and reduce stress for the whole family. In practice, you may be the person who helps a client see that care is not just a medical issue. It is a housing, family, and money issue too."
