        "content": "Long-term care planning usually starts with three areas: **personal planning**, **financial planning**, and **housing considerations**. Personal planning asks where the client wants care and who may help. Financial planning asks how care might be paid for and what coverage already exists. Housing planning asks whether the current home can support safe living if needs change. These three parts work together, so you should not treat them as separate sales topics. A client may have the money to stay home only if the home can be modified. Or the client may need a different living arrangement if family help is limited. That is why a good planning conversation looks at the whole situation, not just one policy."
