    "heading": "4.1.3.1 Understanding your Client",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Understanding your client means more than collecting basic facts. You need to know the client’s budget, family situation, and likely future changes. Many consumers cannot tell whether an agent title or designation means real LTC expertise, so they rely on you to explain the policy in plain language. That makes your job important. If you focus only on the sale, you may miss the client’s real risk. If you focus only on price, you may miss whether the coverage will still be useful later."
      },
      {
        "type": "important_callout",
        "label": "Common Mistake",
