      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Clients plan better when they know where to look for help. Good resources include state or local aging agencies, State Health Insurance Assistance Programs, Aging and Disability Resource Centers, and the Eldercare Locator for local services. For financial questions, clients can use MyMoney.gov, NAIC shopper’s guides, and their state insurance department. For housing and future care planning, the Administration on Aging, HUD, AHRQ, the American Bar Association, and Caring Connections can help with home changes, advance directives, and legal planning. These resources matter because long-term care planning is not only about insurance. It also involves services, housing, and legal choices."
